    std::string getTitle() const { return title; }
    std::string getAuthor() const { return author; }
    std::string getSummary() const { return summary; }
};
```

Next, we'll add a `isSameAs` method to compare the title, author, and summary of two books and return true if they match, false otherwise:

```cpp
bool isSameAs(const Book& other) const {
    return (title == other.title && author == other.author && summary == other.summary);
}
```

Now, let's create three instances of our `Book` class:

